{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2605.23464","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2605.23464","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2605.23464","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2605.23464","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2605.23464"}],"creators":[{"name":"Long, Alexander","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Alexander","familyName":"Long","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Koneputugodage, Chamin Hewa","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Chamin Hewa","familyName":"Koneputugodage","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Ajanthan, Thalaiyasingam","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Thalaiyasingam","familyName":"Ajanthan","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zuo, Yan","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yan","familyName":"Zuo","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Avraham, Gil","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Gil","familyName":"Avraham","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Shevchenko, Violetta","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Violetta","familyName":"Shevchenko","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Dolatabadi, Hadi Mohaghegh","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Hadi Mohaghegh","familyName":"Dolatabadi","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Ramasinghe, Sameera","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Sameera","familyName":"Ramasinghe","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Unextractable Protocol Models: Collaborative Training and Inference without Weight Materialization"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Machine Learning (cs.LG)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-05-22T10:24:57Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-05-25T00:39:53Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-05","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"We consider a decentralized setup in which the participants collaboratively train and serve a large neural network, and where each participant only processes a subset of the model. In this setup, we explore the possibility of unmaterializable weights, where a full weight set is never available to any one participant. We introduce Unextractable Protocol Models (UPMs): a training and inference framework that leverages the sharded model setup to ensure model shards (i.e., subsets) held by participants are incompatible at different time steps. UPMs periodically inject time-varying, random, invertible transforms at participant boundaries; preserving the overall network function yet rendering cross-time assemblies incoherent. On Qwen-2.5-0.5B and Llama-3.2-1B, 10,000 transforms leave FP32 perplexity unchanged ($Δ$PPL $\u0026lt; 0.01$; Jensen-Shannon drift $\u0026lt; 4 \\times 10^{-5}$), and we show how to control growth for lower precision datatypes. Applying a transform every 30s adds 3% latency, 0.1% bandwidth, and 10% GPU-memory overhead at inference, while training overhead falls to 1.6% time and $\u0026lt; 1$% memory. We consider several attacks, showing that the requirements of direct attacks are impractical and easy to defend against, and that gradient-based fine-tuning of stitched partitions consumes $\\geq 60$% of the tokens required to train from scratch. By enabling models to be collaboratively trained yet not extracted, UPMs make it practical to embed programmatic incentive mechanisms in community-driven decentralized training.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"Accepted at NeurIPS 2025. 34 pages, 6 figures (5 in main body, 1 in appendix). Alexander Long and Chamin Hewa Koneputugodage contributed equally","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.23464","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-05-25T01:54:30.000Z","registered":"2026-05-25T01:54:30.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-05-25T01:54:30.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2605.23464","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[]}}}}